@startuml
|Primary CDN Web Server (WS)|
start
:Monitor load / detect hotspot (flash crowd);
if (Exceptional circumstances\nand cannot handle workload?) then (yes)
:Initiate peering trigger request;

|Mediator (Primary CDN)|
:Receive initialization request;
:Obtain resource & access info from Service Registry (SR);
:Obtain SLAs/policies from Policy Repository (PR);
:Generate service requirements\n(based on current circumstance and customer SLA);
:Apply visibility/privacy constraints\n(divergent policies);

|Peering Agent (PA - Primary CDN)|
:Receive service requirements from Mediator;
:Discover potential peer CDNs\n(predict performance; handle limited info sharing);
if (Preexisting peering arrangements exist?) then (yes)
:Return preexisting peering arrangements;
else (no)
:Perform short-term negotiations\nwith external peer PAs;
endif

|External Peer CDN(s) PA|
:Exchange policy/resource info\nand service requirements with Primary PA;
:Respond with offered resources / terms;

|Peering Agent (PA - Primary CDN)|
:Collect peer offers / candidate peers;
if (Any CDN interested / acceptable offer?) then (yes)
:Select peer CDN(s) to establish peering;

|Mediator (Primary CDN)|
:Configure CDN peering protocols\nat conduits of respective CDNs;
:Advertise configurations via inter-PA communication\n(topology, proximity, capability, performance);
:Enable exchange of content availability info;
:Define request-routing/redirection policies\nper peering protocols;

|Primary CDN Web Server (WS)|
:Ensure delivery of content to end-users\nbased on negotiated policies;

fork
|SLA Allocator (Primary CDN)|
:Provision & reserve WS resources\n(CPU/bandwidth/storage) for local and delegated SLAs;
:Enforce SLA terms;
fork again
|Primary CDN Web Server (WS)|
:Perform on-demand caching,\ncontent selection, and routing;
fork again
|Mediator (Primary CDN)|
:Control portion of web traffic redirected to peers;
:Control which content is replicated at peers\nand replication policies used;
end fork

|Operational Management (Participating CDNs)|
:Deploy and administer functional policies;
:Cooperate to execute common goals;
:Exchange accounting information for billing\nbased on negotiated relationships;

|Mediator (Primary CDN)|
if (Sufficient resources acquired\nto meet customer SLA?) then (yes)
:Peering arrangement becomes operational;
else (no)
:Re-negotiate by tuning negotiated relationships\nand reconsidering service requirements;
-> :Receive service requirements from Mediator;
endif

|Operational Management (Participating CDNs)|
if (Need disband or re-arrangement?) then (yes)
:Evaluate conditions:\n(a) circumstances no longer hold\n(b) no longer beneficial\n(c) need expansion for additional load\n(d) contributions not met;
if (Re-arrange within negotiated relationship?) then (yes)
:Re-arrange peering arrangement\n(e.g., expand resources / adjust contributions);
else (no)
:Disband peering arrangement;
endif
endif

stop

else (no)
:Continue normal content delivery locally;
stop
endif
@enduml